  "goodToKnow": "Der Partisan (die Partisanin) is a partisan or guerrilla fighter, especially resistance fighters against occupying forces in WWII in Yugoslavia, Italy, the Soviet Union and elsewhere. In German it doesn't mean a party supporter (that's der Anhänger). Wehrmacht crimes in so-called Partisanenbekämpfung were exposed in the 1990s Wehrmachtsausstellung. It's declined weakly: den Partisanen. Plural: die Partisanen."
